{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>בסד</b> — like: ושדת אותם בסיד, that all my paths be seen in it. And Rabbenu Hai, of blessed memory, said: that it is a fetter, from the words of our Rabbis, of blessed memory." "<b>על שרשי רגלי</b> — on the roots of my feet You set a line and boundary, and it is an allusion to a human being."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {0 "Resolved רבינו האי ז\"ל as Rabbenu Hai of blessed memory, the 11th-century geonic figure."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:02:33.467118361Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}